  "finding": "Of 1,974,976 pooled ATAC intervals only 684,673 are distinct coordinates, a duplication factor of 2.8846. scripts/enhancer_maxdata.py iterates the pooled intervals without deduplication, so a region called in k experiments contributes k training rows. The reported growth of the enhancer training set therefore overstates the growth in distinct accessible regions.",
  "leakage": "This does not create train/test leakage. Splits are held out by chromosome, so every copy of a duplicated region falls on the same side of the split."
